{"data": [{"author_id": "39125788", "created_at": "2026-10-26T20:50:47.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2114822071016398918"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/OPgInkfpXm", "end": 304, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/emollick/status/2114822071016398918/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2114821666912006144", "start": 281, "url": "https://t.co/OPgInkfpXm"}, {"display_url": "pic.x.com/OPgInkfpXm", "end": 304, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/emollick/status/2114822071016398918/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2114821761296388096", "start": 281, "url": "https://t.co/OPgInkfpXm"}]}, "id": "2114822071016398918", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 4, "impression_count": 3076, "like_count": 29, "quote_count": 2, "reply_count": 10, "retweet_count": 2}, "text": "I had GPT-6 Pro revisit the cool finding that violent video games reduce crime, as people stay home playing them. It downloaded fresh crime data &amp; extended prior work.\n\nYes, GTA V's 2013 launch was linked with a dip in violence internationally. Other games are more ambiguous. https://t.co/OPgInkfpXm", "url": "https://x.com/emollick/status/2114822071016398918"}, {"author_id": "1605", "created_at": "2026-10-26T20:37:05.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2114818620782248024"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "x.com/OpenAI/status/…", "end": 137, "expanded_url": "https://twitter.com/OpenAI/status/2114780711664398349", "start": 114, "url": "https://t.co/TbpHp75Os0"}]}, "id": "2114818620782248024", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 60, "impression_count": 59230, "like_count": 861, "quote_count": 21, "reply_count": 181, "retweet_count": 48}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2114780711664398349", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "6.1 Terra is here! It is good at a lot of things, but we are especially excited for this new era of computer use. https://t.co/TbpHp75Os0", "url": "https://x.com/sama/status/2114818620782248024"}, {"author_id": "332617373", "created_at": "2026-10-26T20:24:23.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2114815424059871727"], "entities": {"hashtags": [{"end": 94, "start": 86, "tag": "economy"}, {"end": 103, "start": 95, "tag": "markets"}, {"end": 109, "start": 104, "tag": "tech"}, {"end": 113, "start": 110, "tag": "ai"}, {"end": 137, "start": 114, "tag": "ArtificialIntelligence"}], "mentions": [{"end": 143, "id": "20402945", "start": 138, "username": "CNBC"}, {"end": 155, "id": "404422077", "start": 144, "username": "SquawkCNBC"}], "urls": [{"description": "Mohamed El-Erian, The Wharton School Rene Kern professor and Allianz chief economic advisor, joins 'Squawk Box' to discuss the latest market trends, differentiation in the AI trade, state of the economy, the Fed's inflation fight, and more.", "display_url": "cnbc.com/video/2026/10/…", "end": 85, "expanded_url": "https://www.cnbc.com/video/2026/10/26/mohamed-el-erian-its-a-good-thing-were-seeing-differentiation-in-ai.html", "images": [{"height": 1080, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2114815431492218880/cnuVhRnE?format=jpg&name=orig", "width": 1920}, {"height": 150, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2114815431492218880/cnuVhRnE?format=jpg&name=150x150", "width": 150}], "start": 62, "status": 200, "title": "Mohamed El-Erian: It's a good thing we're seeing differentiation in AI", "unwound_url": "https://www.cnbc.com/video/2026/10/26/mohamed-el-erian-its-a-good-thing-were-seeing-differentiation-in-ai.html", "url": "https://t.co/H4Bi8bjTXe"}]}, "id": "2114815424059871727", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 5, "impression_count": 9095, "like_count": 18, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 4, "retweet_count": 1}, "text": "A clip from this morning's conversation on CNBC's Squawk Box.\nhttps://t.co/H4Bi8bjTXe\n#economy #markets #tech #ai #ArtificialIntelligence @CNBC @SquawkCNBC", "url": "https://x.com/elerianm/status/2114815424059871727"}, {"author_id": "279036722", "created_at": "2026-10-26T19:23:06.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2114800001259839710"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/JJEaRQPwVo", "end": 293, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/jasonfurman/status/2114800001259839710/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2114799626318495744", "start": 270, "url": "https://t.co/JJEaRQPwVo"}]}, "id": "2114800001259839710", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 3, "impression_count": 6920, "like_count": 27, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 8, "retweet_count": 4}, "text": "I've seen speculation AI anxieties are behind negative sentiment. Zero evidence for that:\n\n1. Negativity pre-dates AI.\n\n2. People much more negative about prices than jobs.\n\n3. Negativity same across education/age/income groups\n\n4. Negativity much worse in US but AI is https://t.co/JJEaRQPwVo", "url": "https://x.com/jasonfurman/status/2114800001259839710"}, {"author_id": "279036722", "created_at": "2026-10-26T18:11:41.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2114782030864986353"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/f1OrnQB0Cs", "end": 302, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/jasonfurman/status/2114782030864986353/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2114772192915267584", "start": 279, "url": "https://t.co/f1OrnQB0Cs"}]}, "id": "2114782030864986353", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 49, "impression_count": 21804, "like_count": 145, "quote_count": 11, "reply_count": 18, "retweet_count": 19}, "text": "People in rich countries are unhappy. In the US they're truly miserable.\n\nSentiment fell more in the US since 2019 than any other country.\n\nUS sentiment at the 0th percentile of pre-COVID history, others generally around 25th percentile.\n\nAnd our economy doing better than most! https://t.co/f1OrnQB0Cs", "url": "https://x.com/jasonfurman/status/2114782030864986353"}, {"author_id": "332617373", "created_at": "2026-10-26T17:29:47.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2114771487924367576"], "entities": {"hashtags": [{"end": 221, "start": 214, "tag": "brazil"}, {"end": 227, "start": 222, "tag": "lula"}, {"end": 238, "start": 228, "tag": "bolsonaro"}]}, "id": "2114771487924367576", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 45, "impression_count": 47724, "like_count": 705, "quote_count": 6, "reply_count": 85, "retweet_count": 105}, "text": "The massive magnitude of today’s selloff in Brazilian assets is less about Brazil’s underlying outlook and more about just how confident—and wrong—the consensus view on finance was with respect to a Bolsonaro win.\n#brazil #lula #bolsonaro", "url": "https://x.com/elerianm/status/2114771487924367576"}, {"author_id": "1214528593", "created_at": "2026-10-26T17:07:06.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2114765776741974191"], "entities": {"mentions": [{"end": 251, "id": "252946959", "start": 238, "username": "rahul1987iit"}], "urls": [{"display_url": "x.com/averiorg/statu…", "end": 302, "expanded_url": "https://twitter.com/averiorg/status/2114764187721171052", "start": 279, "url": "https://t.co/fCUZOokdJD"}]}, "id": "2114765776741974191", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 5, "impression_count": 1390, "like_count": 37, "quote_count": 1, "reply_count": 10, "retweet_count": 4}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2114764187721171052", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "Excited to share the results of a recent pilot project with Amazon!\n\nCompanies use private safety evaluations to make decisions with big public consequences. \n\nOur review led to several improvements in Amazon’s internal evals.\n\nThanks to @rahul1987iit for collaboration on this: https://t.co/fCUZOokdJD", "url": "https://x.com/Miles_Brundage/status/2114765776741974191"}, {"author_id": "26538229", "created_at": "2026-10-26T16:36:36.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2114758101316288555"], "entities": {"urls": [{"description": "The Federal Reserve Board of Governors in Washington DC.", "display_url": "federalreserve.gov", "end": 248, "expanded_url": "https://www.federalreserve.gov", "images": [{"height": 800, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2113100610958467072/fFh4Mv1q?format=jpg&name=orig", "width": 800}, {"height": 150, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2113100610958467072/fFh4Mv1q?format=jpg&name=150x150", "width": 150}], "start": 225, "status": 200, "title": "Home", "unwound_url": "https://www.federalreserve.gov", "url": "https://t.co/fXt6ew8I9A"}, {"display_url": "pic.x.com/aOhwLUfWan", "end": 273, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/federalreserve/status/2114758101316288555/video/1", "media_key": "13_2114757670116724736", "start": 250, "url": "https://t.co/aOhwLUfWan"}]}, "id": "2114758101316288555", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 2, "impression_count": 19703, "like_count": 22, "quote_count": 2, "reply_count": 15, "retweet_count": 4}, "text": "Be suspicious of unexpected emails claiming to be from the Federal Reserve. Scammers send fake fraud alerts and scare tactics to steal your financial information. To learn about protecting yourself and your loved ones, visit https://t.co/fXt6ew8I9A. https://t.co/aOhwLUfWan", "url": "https://x.com/federalreserve/status/2114758101316288555"}, {"author_id": "612896910", "created_at": "2026-10-26T15:31:03.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2114741606561497579"], "entities": {"hashtags": [{"end": 101, "start": 93, "tag": "BLSdata"}], "urls": [{"description": "The .gov means it's official. Federal government websites often end in .gov or .mil. Before sharing sensitive information, make sure you're on a federal government site. The site is secure. The https:// ensures that you are connecting to the official website and that any information you provide is encrypted and transmitted securely. In September 2026, unemployment rates in North Dakota and South Dakota were among the lowest, at 2.2 percent and 2.0 percent, respectively. Nebraska, Hawaii, New Hampshire", "display_url": "bls.gov/opub/ted/2026/…", "end": 92, "expanded_url": "https://www.bls.gov/opub/ted/2026/unemployment-rates-in-the-dakotas-among-the-lowest-in-september-2026.htm", "images": [{"height": 126, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2114741618297171968/OMCINDgm?format=png&name=orig", "width": 228}, {"height": 126, "url": "https://